---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import DevNote from '../components/DevNote.astro';
import site from '../content/site.json';
import { url } from '../lib/url.js';

const model = site.credentials.aircraftModel?.startsWith('TODO') ? null : site.credentials.aircraftModel;
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="A one-person aerial photography service in South Wales. CAA Flyer ID and Operator ID held, insured, flying a sub-250g aircraft in Open category subcategory A1."
>
  <article>
    <header class="section head">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Kite Aerial is one person and one small aircraft.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Named after the red kite, which does the same job with better equipment and no paperwork.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="who">
      <div class="wrap cols">
        <h2 id="who">Who's flying</h2>
        <div class="colbody">

        <p>
          Hi, I'm Keshav. I'm an engineer, photographer, and UAV enthusiast. I am on a mission to help property owners upscale their listings and their perceived value through professional aerial photoshoots. I understand that not all properties benefit from aerial shots; hence, I also provide consultation to seek your best interest.
        </p>

        <p>
          I have flown several house shoots around the UK, including Swansea and Gower. To help you visualise my work, I have made a case study and covered
          from top to bottom — multiple angles, several heights, and an orbit on video. That one is
          <a href={url("/case-study")}>written up as a case study</a>, because a full sequence shows more about how
          somebody works than a grid of best shots ever does.
        </p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="paperwork">
      <div class="wrap cols">
        <h2 id="paperwork">The paperwork</h2>
        <div class="colbody">
        <p>
          I hold a CAA Flyer ID and a CAA Operator ID. {site.credentials.insurance} The aircraft is sub-250g and
          in the UK0/C0 class{model ? `, ${model}` : ''}, which puts the work in the Open category, subcategory A1.
        </p>
        <p>
          A1 is the part that matters commercially: it lets me fly in residential and built-up areas rather than
          keeping a hundred and fifty metres clear of them. That is the difference between photographing a house on
          a normal street and not being able to.
        </p>
        <p>
          I check airspace, land ownership and any site-specific permissions before quoting a date. There is a
          <a href={url("/where-we-fly")}>longer page about that</a> if you want to see the working.
        </p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="not">
      <div class="wrap cols">
        <h2 id="not">What I don't do</h2>
        <div class="colbody">
        <p>
          I don't do survey work, and I'd be careful of anyone with a drone this size who says they do. The camera
          has a rolling shutter, which bends geometry slightly while the sensor reads out, and no amount of
          processing fully removes that. So I will happily build you a 3D visualisation of a building or a plot.
          I will not put a measurement on it and call it accurate.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also don't publish numbers about how much faster aerial photographs sell a house. The figure that gets
          quoted everywhere traces back to a marketing blog and American data, and I would rather show you a
          property from a hundred metres up and let you decide.
        </p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cost">
      <div class="wrap cols">
        <h2 id="cost">On the price</h2>
        <div class="colbody">
        <p>
          A listing shoot costs roughly what a good Gower let takes in a night or two in August. I'd put it on that
          side of the ledger rather than filing it with the marketing costs — the photographs stay useful for as
          long as the property does.
        </p>
        <p><a class="btn" href={url("/#enquiry")}>Send an enquiry</a></p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .head h1 {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 20ch;
  }

  .cols {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem 3rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 16rem) minmax(0, 38rem);
    }
  }

  .colbody > * + * {
    margin-top: 1.15rem;
  }

  .colbody p {
    line-height: 1.62;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 38rem;
  }
</style>
